                            <a name="comment2732"></a>
<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: Sunday Reading
</h4>

<p>
My editor forwarded to me a story that appeared on the front page of Sunday's Washington Post. It shows neighbors finally getting to know each other. The excuse? One of the California fires burned their homes down. <br />
<br />
The story is exquisite. The reporter, Tamara Jones, plays brilliantly with chronology, and she mentions so many symbolic details that as I read it I got the chills again and again, and she describes the neighbors clearly, showing changes in them over time, and, and, and . . . most importantly, she humanizes for us, down to the street level, a development that's otherwise so vast that we've struggled fathom it. And gosh, the story is newsworthy! I love it. <br />
<br />
http://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/content/article/2007/10/27/AR2007102701173.html
</p>
<div class="posted">Posted by:


		<a href="jordanino@gmail.com">Jordan</a>
	

